docs/requirements/decisions/product-capability-release-playbook-lineage-execution-plan.md:146:| M1 Capability Release Schema | There is no first-class non-runtime product capability release record, and no read-time enforcement of its non-authoritative status. | `ProductCapabilityReleaseRecord` schema + `.lattice/capability-releases.jsonl` ledger (git-tracked) + fail-closed reader + gate-import guard test. | Unit tests: parse, deterministic `capabilityDigest`/`idempotencyKey`/id (fixed input→value), idempotent append, malformed-row rejection, fail-closed on `gateEvidence:true`/non-`non_authoritative` rows, guard test that no gate path imports the reader. |
docs/requirements/decisions/product-capability-release-playbook-lineage-execution-plan.md-147-| M2 DONE Capability Classification | DONE distinguishes runtime semver vs artifact release, but not reusable product capability release. | A **pure classifier fn in `core/`** (mirroring `selectArtifactReleasePathsV1`) invoked from **both** DONE completion sites. | Fixtures for B-785e-like docs/experiments, plain docs, runtime code, story-metadata-only; conservative-uncertain → advisory + no record. |
docs/requirements/decisions/product-capability-release-playbook-lineage-execution-plan.md-148-| M3 Release Binding | Artifact releases and capability releases can drift, and recovery re-merge must not duplicate. | Capability record binds `storyId`, `mainCommit` (provenance), `artifactReleaseId?`, `artifactSetDigest?`, `capabilityId`, `capabilityVersion`, `capabilityDigest`, `changedPaths`; dedup on a merge-stable key. | Smoke proves deterministic binding and **no duplicate record when re-run with a different `mainCommit`** (recovery path). |
docs/requirements/decisions/product-capability-release-playbook-lineage-execution-plan.md-149-| M4 Playbook Lineage Binding | Candidate playbooks know only `DONE-EXPERIENCE`, not the capability they came from. | `PlaybookLineage` gains **optional** capability fields (existing 3-field rows stay valid); DONE candidate ingest attaches them when a capability release exists; idempotency defined on the stable source key, not digest equality. | `PBP-882`-style fixture includes `lineage.capabilityReleaseId`/`artifactReleaseId`; pre-existing 3-field lineage still parses; re-apply is a no-op that does not trip stale-proposal rejection. |
